  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a convex relaxation approach combined with Lagrangian optimization to tackle the non-convex nature of the overlap integral. By transforming the problem into a convex framework, we aim to find a lower bound on C\u2085, ensuring feasible solutions while addressing computational constraints.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^n, \u2211h = n/2\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k (\u03a3 h_i(1 - h_{i+k})) * (2/n)\n- Relaxation: Transform into a convex form by considering each shift k as a constraint, aiming to minimize the maximum overlap.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialization: Start with initial_h_values and scale to n=100.\nb. Convex Relaxation: Formulate as a convex problem with constraints for each shift.\nc. Lagrangian Optimization: Use multipliers to handle constraints and apply subgradient methods.\nd. Iterative Refinement: Adjust Lagrange multipliers and update h iteratively.\ne. Projection: Ensure feasibility through iterative redistribution after each update.\nf. Termination: Stop when budget exhausted or convergence achieved.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Choose Lagrange multiplier update rules based on dual ascent.\n- Vary shift constraints for diverse exploration.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nEstimate time for each step, prioritizing efficient subgradient updates and early termination.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nEnsure h satisfies constraints and validate C\u2085 with the evaluator.",
